diff --git a/DOCS/man/input.rst b/DOCS/man/input.rst
index 77500750a..da12a7fa6 100644
--- a/DOCS/man/input.rst
+++ b/DOCS/man/input.rst
@@ -1525,6 +1525,37 @@ Screenshot Commands
         MPV_FORMAT_NODE_MAP
             "filename"    MPV_FORMAT_STRING
 
+``capture-output <filename> [<redraw>]`` (mpv-ht, gpu-next/D3D11)
+    Arm a one-shot, lossless capture of the next live backbuffer before Present.
+    Unlike ``screenshot``, this does not render a separate image, change output
+    precision, or bypass the normal frame cache. All video and OSD already drawn
+    into that buffer are included. Windows composition and display processing
+    happen later and are not captured.
+
+    The result is an accepted request sequence, not completion. Poll the
+    ``output-capture`` property for the same sequence and state ``complete`` or
+    ``error``. Only one request may be pending. The path must be writable and
+    must not already exist; it is not expanded as a screenshot filename template.
+    An empty filename cancels a pending request and removes its partial file.
+    Seek/reset and VO teardown also cancel pending requests. Unsupported output
+    backends reject the command; there is no fallback to rerendered screenshots.
+
+    ``redraw`` defaults to ``yes`` and requests an ordinary cached redraw, so
+    paused content can be captured. ``no`` waits for the next naturally rendered
+    frame; a paused/minimized output may remain pending until cancelled. There
+    is no continuous capture or readback while inactive. A requested capture can
+    stall the VO for GPU synchronization and disk writing; use for diagnostics,
+    not frame-by-frame recording.
+
+    The file contains ``MPVCAP1`` and a newline, a UTF-8 JSON metadata line, then
+    tightly packed native framebuffer rows. It is not a PNG. Metadata describes
+    dimensions, row length, native format/type, little-endian component bits and
+    sample order, row orientation, color primaries/transfer, frame ID, PTS and
+    request sequence. No quantization or color conversion is performed.
+    Captures are bounded to 512 MiB of pixel data. The mpv-ht
+    ``analysis/read-output-capture.js`` reader supports native UNORM and float
+    output for automated pixel assertions.
+
 ``screenshot-to-file <filename> [<flags>]``
     Take a screenshot and save it to a given file. The format of the file will
     be guessed by the extension (and ``--screenshot-format`` is ignored - the
